From 17b1b749953a9b13706d46a9f1f7f0c1767e47b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 07:24:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 11/15] rdna-boosts: block 11: qwen4exp (model,
 hyper-connections, lazy reader, QSA/indexer)

The qwen4exp (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next) architecture support, split out of the old
block 10 (r109) so the model graph, the sparse-attention op and the
hyper-connections no longer share a commit with the slab, the fusion dispatcher
and the async input ring.  The tree is unchanged: block 10 plus this commit is
exactly what the old block 10 carried.

Contents:

- src/models/qwen4exp.cpp: the model, the HC (hyper-connection) graph, the MTP
  draft head, the PLE gather, the QSA selection/attention graph
  (build_qsa_store_k / build_qsa_top_k / build_attn_qsa) and the QSA arm policy.
- QSA/indexer: fattn-qsa.{cu,cuh}, fattn-qsa3.cu, indexer-score.{cu,cuh},
  indexer-topk.{cu,cuh}, the 4-head WMMA indexer scorer in lightning-indexer.cu,
  with the CUDA dispatch (GGML_OP_FLASH_ATTN_QSA / INDEXER_TOPK / INDEXER_SCORE /
  INDEXER_FILL) and their CPU references; the keys-only indexer cache
  (LLAMA_QSA_KEYS_ONLY, no V tensor at all) in llama-memory-hybrid-idx and the
  v_enabled parameter on llama_kv_cache.
- HC ops GGML_OP_HC_MIX / HC_COMBINE (dispatch, supports_op, the Meta split
  states, the hc_combine_mix / hc_mix / hc_combine_norm / hc_gate_mix fusion
  arms and the HC16 planar layout) in hc-mix.{cu,cuh} and hyperconn.{cu,cuh}.
- The managed lazy reader (llama-lazy-reader) and the loader's managed_budget
  (LLAMA_LAZY_BUF_MB, TENSOR_SKIP_MANAGED, lazy_read::add_range) for the PLE
  n-gram table; off by default (it measured slower than both the mmap and the
  resident path on gfx1151).
- The QSA/HC op definitions in ggml.h / ggml.c, the scheduler op allowlists, the
  CPU references, and the qwen4exp tensor-split arch gate in llama-arch.cpp (with
  the ggml-hip CMakeLists publishing GGML_USE_HIP to the main libraries so the
  dynamic-backend build reads it).
- The qwen4exp MTP draft context gets a hybrid-idx memory instead of a plain KV
  cache (LLAMA_MTP_SPARSE=0 restores the dense draft), and llama_memory_recurrent
  stops warning about the speculative verify positions for a context whose
  recurrent filter matches nothing.
- Loader/user-path fix: TENSOR_READ_LAZY is only consulted when the loader has
  files (the llama_model_init_from_user path has nothing to lazy-read from).
- The qwen4exp-family fusion arms that live in this block's own TUs, and the
  graph-optimizer passes they need: the HC_BLK16/RES16 BF16-stream marks and
  their alloc deps, and the prefill indexer relu-sum alloc dep.
- Tests: test-hc-mix and test_flash_attn_qsa in test-backend-ops (the QSA CPU
  oracle: `test-backend-ops -o FLASH_ATTN_QSA`, 18/18 minimum), test-lazy-reader,
  and the lazy_buf_size handover in test-llama-archs.

Split note (r109): the infrastructure this block is built on -- the slab, the
fusion dispatcher TU, the async input ring, the GDN/MMB/HC16 kernel work -- is
block 10 and is listed there.  A qwen4exp-only change that is implemented inside
a general kernel TU (the GDN gate/beta BF16 fusion, the HC16 MMB BF16 streams,
the weighted-down reduction, the PLE conv fusion) deliberately stays with that
TU in block 10; only the code that needs this block's own symbols is here.

- The separate-tensor (pre-#31028) HC mixer emits its inject product right
  behind the down product, i.e. adjacent in the graph, and expands both: the two
  BF16 GEMMs read the same F32 `xn`, and the CUDA BF16 src1 cache (block 10)
  only holds one converted tensor.  #31028's ordering (inject last, after the
  gate product whose src1 is the silu output, which evicts the entry) converted
  the whole [hc*n_embd, n_tok] tensor twice per mixer -- measured on Flash-Next
  GSQ-IQ3_XXS as 2x the F32->BF16 `convert_unary_cont_vec4` launches and +3.4 %
  prefill when restored (issue #226 follow-up).

R175 amendment: the QSA combine launch passes the new `block_q8_1 * q8` argument
of `flash_attn_combine_results` (added by block 10's FA-combine Q8_1 publish) as
`nullptr` -- QSA's output is not fed to a quantized matmul, so it publishes
nothing.
